# mt-st configuration file
#
# This file defines settings for the mt-st tape device driver.
# It allows setting default behaviors for tape operations such as buffering,
# read-ahead strategies, and asynchronous writes.
#
# Common definitions to be applied to all tape devices
# (This is the driver's default)
{#
  Space-separated list of tape device options.
  Available options typically include:
  - buffer-writes: Enable buffered writes for better performance.
  - read-ahead: Enable read-ahead caching to improve sequential read speeds.
  - async-writes: Enable asynchronous write operations to reduce blocking.
#}
{buffer-writes read-ahead async-writes}